{"type":"standard","title":"Paul LePage","displaytitle":"<span lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><span class=\"mw-page-title-main\">Paul LePage</span></span>","namespace":{"id":0,"text":""},"wikibase_item":"Q881196","titles":{"canonical":"Paul_LePage","normalized":"Paul LePage","display":"<span lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><span class=\"mw-page-title-main\">Paul LePage</span></span>"},"pageid":27678925,"thumbnail":{"source":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/50/Paul_LePage_by_Gage_Skidmore.jpg/330px-Paul_LePage_by_Gage_Skidmore.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","width":330,"height":448},"originalimage":{"source":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/5/50/Paul_LePage_by_Gage_Skidmore.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","width":2408,"height":3272},"lang":"en","dir":"ltr","revision":"1377442478","tid":"0594833a-bbfb-11f1-9067-914765a94b9d","timestamp":"2026-09-29T11:43:43Z","description":"Governor of Maine from 2011 to 2019","description_source":"local","content_urls":{"desktop":{"page":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Paul_LePage","revisions":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Paul_LePage?action=history","edit":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Paul_LePage?action=edit","talk":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Talk:Paul_LePage"},"mobile":{"page":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Paul_LePage","revisions":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:History/Paul_LePage","edit":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Paul_LePage?action=edit","talk":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Talk:Paul_LePage"}},"extract":"Paul Richard LePage is an American businessman and politician who served as the 74th governor of Maine from 2011 to 2019. A member of the Republican Party, he previously served as the mayor of Waterville, Maine, from 2004 to 2011 and as a city councilor for Waterville from 1998 to 2002.","extract_html":"<p><b>Paul Richard LePage</b> is an American businessman and politician who served as the 74th governor of Maine from 2011 to 2019. A member of the Republican Party, he previously served as the mayor of Waterville, Maine, from 2004 to 2011 and as a city councilor for Waterville from 1998 to 2002.</p>"}